<p>Filmlog is the app for movie and cinema lovers — personal, offline and ad-free. Built by one person since 2013 and paid for by the people who use it, it arrived this week on the Mac as a native app, joining iPhone, iPad and a watchlist companion on Apple TV. The new Mac app is not a phone app in a window; it&#8217;s the real deal. It&#8217;s got a sidebar for your sections, a detail pane beside the list, menu commands for what you do most, and keyboard shortcuts for the rest. Soundtracks play right inside Filmlog, and your watching habits come to the desktop as widgets.</p>
<p>Search 315,000 movies, 464,000 people and 58,000 cinemas offline, follow new theatrical releases, plan with your watchlist and challenges, listen to soundtracks from Apple Music, and keep a personal diary of what you watched, with whom and where. The catalog goes deep: find a movie by who’s in the story and where it’s set, by the book it was based on and what it’s about. Follow the people you care about, and their upcoming movies appear in your releases.</p>
<p>The watchlist, the diary, soundtracks and export are free; Filmlog Plus adds the full search and releases, multi-device support, statistics and widgets, the Claude Desktop extension, importing your history, watchlist and ratings from Letterboxd, IMDb, Filmtipset or any CSV, and more. Subscription or one-time purchase; every plan includes Family Sharing.</p>
